leads.description:
shc simply wraps a shell script in C and turns it into a binary.
As a result, if you monitor the kernel with tools like auditd or bpftrace, the shell script is still visible.<p>I solved this by combining a shell interpreter (such as BusyBox) and the shell script into a single static binary.
Because the shell script is never passed to the operating system&#x27;s &#x2F;bin&#x2F;sh or &#x2F;bin&#x2F;
